  "about": "Codex CLI 0.171.0 PreToolUse and PostToolUse payloads run through the unchanged Claude plugin hooks. Read by src/test/agent-tool-aliases.test.mts. expect.decision is deny (stdout carries a permissionDecision deny), allow (empty stdout, exit 0) or warn (empty stdout, exit 0, stderr says why). Placeholders: <HOME> and <PROJECT> are the per-case temp home and project, <PROJECT_HASH> hashProjectRoot(<PROJECT>). platform win32 or posix limits a case to that host.",
  "sources": {
    "payload": "Verified research, Codex entry, hook_payload_example: required keys from codex-rs/hooks/schema/generated/pre-tool-use.command.input.schema.json at rust-v0.171.0 (cwd, hook_event_name, model, permission_mode, session_id, tool_input, tool_name, tool_use_id, transcript_path, turn_id). Bash tool_input is {command}, built from exec_command.rs json!({ \"command\": args.cmd }).",
    "tool_names": "Verified research, Codex entry, tool_names: the shell is \"Bash\" (also PowerShell on Windows); edits and writes are \"apply_patch\" with the full patch text in tool_input.command and the paths only in the *** Add File / *** Update File / *** Delete File headers. exec_command is the model-facing name, normalized to Bash in hook payloads. Skeptic verdict hook_pre_tool: tool names and tool_input.command for both Bash and apply_patch hold.",
    "matcher": "The Claude matcher Bash|PowerShell|Monitor|Edit|MultiEdit|Write|NotebookEdit still matches Bash and apply_patch on Codex (tool_names: the matcher may also say Edit or Write for apply_patch), so the hooks fire; Skill never matches."
  },
